# Harness follow-ups

- `pi_idle.py`: Keep `openai-codex` push-only. Pi 1.1.0's
  `openai-codex-responses.js` sends `prompt_cache_key` but does not apply
  `PI_CACHE_RETENTION`, so scheduling warning and compaction would target a cold
  cache. Revisit when Pi applies `PI_CACHE_RETENTION` in its `openai-codex`
  adapter; check `openai-codex-responses.js` in the installed package.
- `opencode_idle.py`: Clear `_compacting` on the first `session.idle` after the
  compaction part has been seen, even if `POST /summarize` has not returned.
  On 1.18.32 the response beats `session.idle` by only 2–4 ms; if the order
  flips, the user's next prompt is filed as a compaction and one whole idle
  period gets no push, warn or compaction (G2-X N1). Add a test that delivers
  `session.idle` before the POST is released.
- `codex_idle.py`: `compact()` reports `failed: timeout` when an older
  `Context compacted` line scrolls off screen as the new one appears (visible
  pane count does not rise) or when compaction exceeds 60 s. Capture with
  `-S -200`, or also accept "marker visible and `Working (` gone" after a busy
  frame (G2-X N2). Only the report is wrong; the stretch does not loop.
